  "id": "user_task_5",
  "prompt": "I have 4 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) TURN ON LIGHTS: From light worklist `light_jobs_wl2`, turn on each light NOT already on (skip already_on on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists lights already on and out-of-scope 'annex' look-alikes). For each real one, follow its zone to the room, the room to its light fixture, and the fixture to the device id, then switch it on. Then, from worklist `send_notification_wl1`, post the evening-routine status notification: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `set_occupancy_wl1`, record the sunroom occupancy update: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) SECURE DOORS: From lock worklist `lock_jobs_wl2`, lock each door NOT already locked (skip already_locked on its dereferenced record — the list mixes annex look-alikes). For each, follow zone -> room -> lock fixture -> device id, then lock it. Then, from worklist `set_blinds_wl1`, close the living-room blinds: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `unlock_door_wl1`, unlock the service-entrance door for the arriving contractor: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) ENABLE CAMERAS: From camera worklist `camera_jobs_wl2`, enable each camera NOT already enabled (skip already_enabled on its dereferenced record). For each, follow zone -> room -> camera fixture -> device id, then enable it. Then, from worklist `arm_alarm_wl1`, arm the perimeter security in away mode: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `set_lock_autolock_wl1`, set the courtyard-gate auto-relock delay: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) ARM SENSORS: From sensor worklist `sensor_jobs_wl2`, enable each security-zone sensor NOT already enabled (skip already_enabled on its dereferenced record). For each, follow zone -> room -> sensor fixture -> device id, then enable it. Then, from worklist `add_guest_access_wl1`, grant the housekeeper a door PIN: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `disarm_alarm_wl1`, disarm the alarm using the maintenance PIN: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 4 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
